<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls to 7.57 pct on Portugal 10-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield falls to 7.57 pct on Portugal 10-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Treasury's auction of 10 billion escudos of 10-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23/2/06</p>
<p>COUPON: 9.50 pct   AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 7.56925 pct</p>
<p>BID AMOUNT: 61.6 billion escudos</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED YIELD: 7.57 pct MINIMUM ACCEPTED: 7.56</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE: 12/11/96</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 234.01 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
